@fm description | description | The allergen rules for every product sold at Crumbwick Bakery.
# Allergens
s description | Nuts, milk, egg, sesame and gluten are the five allergens that appear in our products.
s description | Gluten appears in every loaf, so the gluten line is printed on every label.
## Labels
s gate{all_label} | Print the allergen label for every new product before it goes on a shelf.
s gate{all_check} | Read the recipe card to the head baker before you print a new label.
s prohibition{all_guess} | Never guess an allergen from the name of a product.
s example | For example, a poppy roll can still carry sesame if it shares a tray with sesame buns.
s rule | Put the label on the front of the sack, not on the back.
## Answering customers
l rule{all_answer} | Say plainly which allergens a product contains
l rule | Offer the allergen folder if the customer asks for more detail
l prohibition{all_free} | Do not say that anything is free of nuts
l description | The allergen folder sits on the counter by the till
## Cross contact
s description | The walnut loaf is baked on its own tray in the small oven.
s rule | Wash the walnut tray in its own sink with its own cloth.
s prohibition | Do not bake a walnut loaf and a sesame bun in the same oven load.
s gate{all_walnut} | Wipe the small oven deck clean before the walnut loaf goes in.
s example | Case: a nut free customer reacted to a bun that was baked after the walnut loaf on a dirty deck.
## Emergencies
s gate{all_ambulance} | Call the emergency number first if a customer reacts to food.
s gate | Tell the shop manager after the call.
s description | The emergency number is written on the wall beside the sconce room door.
s rule | Stay calm and speak clearly.
